        "original_id": "639fbd21-b90a-5ef5-afcb-fc37e923f8bf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Stephen Pearcy, Alexander O'Neal, Al Pitrelli, Hiro Kuretani\n- Bands: Ratt, Vertex, Arcade, Vicious Delite, Nitronic, Danger Danger, Hotshot, Asia, Savatage, Megadeth, Trans-Siberian Orchestra, WXXI, Trancentral Station\n- Roles: musician, singer, songwriter, arranger, guitarist, drummer, founder\n- Places: Natchez, Mississippi\n\nFacts:\n- Alexander O'Neal was born on November 15, 1953, and he is an American R&B singer, songwriter, and arranger from Natchez, Mississippi.\n- Stephen Eric Pearcy was born on July 3, 1956, and he is an American musician known as Stephen Pearcy.\n- Vertex was formed in 1995 and featured singer Stephen Pearcy, guitarist Al Pitrelli, and drummer Hiro Kuretani.\n- Stephen Pearcy is best known as the founder, singer, and songwriter of the heavy metal band Ratt.\n- Stephen Pearcy was also associated with Arcade, Vicious Delite, and Nitronic.\n- Al Pitrelli was also associated with Danger Danger, Hotshot, Alice Cooper, Asia, Savatage, Megadeth, and Trans-Siberian Orchestra.\n- Hiro Kuretani was also associated with WXXI and Trancentral Station.",
